 "description": "The first volume of a ten-part course that takes you from complete beginner to expert in large language models. It explains in plain words what AI, machine learning and LLMs are, how a model predicts the next token, what tokens are, how a whole answer is generated, where LLMs came from, how to write your first good prompts, what LLMs can and cannot do, and how to set up your learning workbench. Every chapter has diagrams, examples you can run, and Check your knowledge questions with answers and explanations.",
